{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"220","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Little Elephant and Triangle"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant is playing with the Cartesian coordinates' system. Most of all he likes playing with integer points. The Little Elephant defines an integer point as a pair of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x; y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ x ≤ w"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ y ≤ h"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, the Little Elephant knows only "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(w + 1)·(h + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct integer points."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant wants to paint a triangle with vertexes at integer points, the triangle's area must be a positive integer. For that, he needs to find the number of groups of three points that form such triangle. At that, the order of points in a group matters, that is, the group of three points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0;0)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0;2)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2;2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" isn't equal to the group "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0;2)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0;0)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2;2)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the Little Elephant to find the number of groups of three integer points that form a nondegenerate triangle with integer area."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A single line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ w, h ≤ 4000)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single output line print an integer — the remainder of dividing the answer to the problem by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(109 + 7)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"36\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"240\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"220D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/220/problem/D"}